{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449150-bagger-hacker-hunting-checks","id":1449150,"title":"Bagger Hacker Hunting Checks?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-20T14:44:46-07:00","id":1449150,"title":"Bagger Hacker Hunting Checks?","content":"I play a Malkavian in a chronicle where the coterie are information brokers in Portland, and she's a hacker, that I'm trying to portray in a very realistic, Mr Robot-style way, so I've focused on aspects like social engineering, darknet networking, phishing etc, rather than random &quot;Hollywood&quot; hacking. But she's also a Bagger. I've stocked up on backgrounds meant to facilitate her aqcuiring blood bags from underworld networks and darknet markets, more precisely Contacts 2 (a hacking network called the Maze), Resources 3 (partly from bitcoin mining/trading), and Mawla 2 (an anarch called Janiz who works with thinblood alchemists to sell blood). Given all that investment in appropriate backgrounds, I feel like they should help somehow when I try to acquire blood through Hunting Checks, and the default hunting difficulty (6) feels very harsh. Whereas other characters in the coterie are alley cats and sirens, and thus would hunt more straightforwardly, both me and the game master feel like my hunting checks should rather represent me ordering blood from Janiz, or stocking up on blood bought form the dark web. But I can't seem to find any good suggestions in the rules for how my backgrounds can aid me in this. Just like the other characters who hunt in the street might get a lowered difficulty due to our domain's Portillion trait, shouldn't I be able to get a lowered difficulty thanks to my contacts or mawla?<br /> <br /> So my questions is: Are there any rules that I've missed for how appropriate backgrounds can lower the difficulty of hunting checks, or otherwise aid in hunting, or do you have any suggestions on how me and my game master might handle this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","user":"Natsymir","date":". 05-20-2021, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","name":"Natsymir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}